  "description": "The top text asks 'what's the difference between the 2?', and the bottom text answers by referring to 'the first one' — which visually corresponds to monkey_1 on the left. The meme uses monkey_1 as the visual representation of the 'first one' in the racist joke, implying it is the one that cannot sing when restrained (i.e., when 'chains' are put on it). This mapping is explicit through the textual reference to 'the first one' and its visual alignment with monkey_1.",
